  "note": "Election of the Whitehead Urban Council, poll due Wednesday 21 May 1958; only six nominations were received for nine seats, so the six were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 8 May 1958, p. 6). Six nominations for nine seats; the report says members who did not send in nomination papers would be invited in order of polling strength at the last election to accept office, and any remaining vacancies filled by co-option. Returned unopposed."
